 e1tc6bzh0"><div class=3D"gamut-1ag67m1-FlexBox e1tc6bzh0"><h1 class=3D"gam=
ut-oqq5yh-StyledText e8i0p5k0">Introducing Jupyter Notebook</h1><p class=3D=
"gamut-1dzl6xd-StyledText e8i0p5k0"><span data-testid=3D"markdown" class=3D=
"styles_markdown__Y5HHD gamut-1leh7be-MarkdownWrapper-spacingNone e1mjarmv0=
" spacing=3D"none">What is Jupyter Notebook? </span></p><div class=3D"gamut=
-b63km8-Box e164dx5n1"><div data-testid=3D"markdown" class=3D"styles_markdo=
wn__Y5HHD styles_darkTheme__sfPfQ e164dx5n0 gamut-1mhtesm-MarkdownWrapper-m=
arkdownStyle-spacingLoose e1mjarmv0" spacing=3D"loose"><h4 id=3D"heading-in=
troduction" class=3D"g-md-h4">Introduction</h4>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Jupyter Notebook (sometimes called IPython Notebook) is=
 a popular way to write and run Python code, especially for data analysis, =
data science and machine learning. Jupyter Notebooks are easy-to-use becaus=
e they let you execute code and review the output quickly. This iterative p=
rocess is central to data analytics and makes it easy to test hypotheses an=
d record the results (just like a notebook). </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">For example, let=E2=80=99s say you are visualizing a da=
taset about life expectancy by country. You only want to show some countrie=
s, but you are not sure which ones to select. With a Jupyter Notebook, you =
can try multiple versions and easily compare. Even better, you have a writt=
en record of what you=E2=80=99ve already tried that you can show a teammate=
 (or your future self). This is just one example of the many benefits of wo=
rking within a notebook-like environment.</p>
<h4 id=3D"heading-getting-familiar-with-jupyter-notebook" class=3D"g-md-h4"=
>Getting Familiar with Jupyter Notebook</h4>
<p class=3D"g-md-p"><img alt=3D"movie showing a Jupyter notebook in action"=
 class=3D"g-md-img" src=3D"https://static-assets.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/Paths/data-=
science-career-path/getting-started-off-platform/sample-anaconda.gif"></p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Above is the Jupyter Notebook interface. A Jupyter Note=
book has two parts:</p>
<ul class=3D"g-md-ul">
<li class=3D"g-md-li">the front-end interface (what you see in the gif)</li=
>
<li class=3D"g-md-li">the back-end kernel</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">The front-end interface loads in a web browser and cons=
ists of =E2=80=9Ccells=E2=80=9D where you enter your code. The browser is j=
ust for display, so you do not need to be connected to the internet. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Jupyter Notebook uses a back-end kernel called IPython.=
 The =E2=80=98I=E2=80=99 stands for =E2=80=98Interactive=E2=80=99, which me=
ans that a program or script can be broken up into smaller pieces, and thos=
e pieces can be run independently from the rest of the program. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">You do not need to worry about the difference between P=
ython and IPython. The important thing to know is that you can run small pi=
eces of code, which can be helpful when working with data.</p>
<h4 id=3D"heading-integrated-development-environments-ides" class=3D"g-md-h=
4">Integrated Development Environments (IDEs)</h4>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">Jupyter Notebook is a type of <a target=3D"_blank" href=
=3D"https://www.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/article/what-is-an-ide" class=3D"g-md-a gamu=
t-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14vpv2g0">Integrated Development Environment (IDE)</a=
>. IDEs are places to write code that offer some supportive features. Almos=
t all IDEs provide syntax highlighting, debugging, and code completion. Jup=
yter Notebook also offers embedded help documentation and introspection (i.=
e., you can check each command=E2=80=99s parameters) and in-line display of=
 charts and images. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">There are many IDEs for writing Python. We recommend Ju=
pyter Notebook because running small experiments is also very helpful when =
learning how to code. </p>
<p class=3D"g-md-p">However, the best way to get familiar with Jupyter Note=
book is to <a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://www.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/article/=
how-to-use-jupyter-notebooks" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14v=
pv2g0">work with it yourself</a>. So without further ado, let=E2=80=99s wal=
k through getting Jupyter Notebook and related tools installed on your comp=
uter in the <a target=3D"_blank" href=3D"https://www.AI Academy by RiWoT.com/article=
s/setting-up-jupyter-notebook" class=3D"g-md-a gamut-1r92bn9-AnchorBase e14=
vpv2g0">next article</a>! </p>
